Content Management Workflow for Non-Technical Staff
Factor	               Traditional WordPress                 	Headless WordPress
Editing Experience  	 Familiar WP admin (ideal for staff)  Same WP admin (no change for staff)
Multi-Platform Sync	   Requires plugins/custom feeds      	Native REST API feeds all platforms
Preview Functionality  Full WYSIWYG preview	            Limited to CMS (no frontend preview)

Development Complexity & Team Skills
Factor	              Traditional WordPress	                       Headless WordPress
Frontend Stack	      PHP/Theme Dev (simple)	                     React/Vue + API integration (complex)
Team Requirements	     WordPress-only devs	                       API + JS framework specialists
Cross-Platform Logic  Duplicate content logic per platform         Single API serves all

Hosting & Infrastructure Costs
Factor           	  Traditional WordPress	       Headless WordPress
Backend Hosting	    Standard WP hosting        	Same WP hosting
Frontend Hosting	  Included	                  Extra costs (app servers, CDN, SSR)
Traffic Scaling	    WP caching plugins	        Static sites (cheaper at scale)

Long-Term Maintenance & Scalability
Factor           	Traditional WordPress	          Headless WordPress
Platform Updates	Risk of theme/plugin conflicts	Frontends update independently
New Platforms	    Requires new WP themes/plugins	Just consume existing API
Performance	      Caching plugins needed	        Fast static sites + CDN caching

Headless should be used because:
Menu changes (e.g., seasonal drinks) update everywhere instantly.
New locations just tap into the same API.
No emergency fixes if WP updates break digital menus.

